   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi all,<div>I was hoping you could help me with this problem.</div><div><br></div><div>I have a variable Y whose shifted version is exponential : p(Y)=lambda exp(-lambda(Y-tau))</div><div>which means that Y-tau~exponential(lambda).</div><div>I am trying to use stan to estimate lambda and tau, but it just blows up.</div><div><br></div><div>This is my code in stan:</div><div><br></div><div><div>data {</div><div>  int&lt;lower=0&gt;      N;<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t</span>            </div><div>  real&lt;lower=0&gt; y[N];<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t\t</span>              </div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>parameters {</div><div>  real&lt;lower=0,upper=10&gt;lambda;<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t\t\t</span>           </div><div>  real                                  tau;<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t\t\t</span>              </div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>model {</div><div>real ytransf[N];</div><div><br></div><div>for(n in 1:N){</div><div>        ytransf[n]&lt;-y[n]-tau;    </div><div>        ytransf[n]~exponential(lambda);</div><div>  }</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>I have also trying to fix lambda to the true value and just estimate tau, but I still get crazy results.</div><div>What is it going on? Anyone who can help?</div><div>It would be very much appreciated.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Laura</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "I6ymdWLQAvgJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-06-24T19:33:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: shifted exponential",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You need to restrict the range of tau:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>transformed data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  min_y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">min_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// ignore parser message about Jacobian adjustment</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tau </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exponential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">lambda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
